TEXT 0 -352 Left 2 ;First-order all-pass with an op amp: R1-C1 is a low-pass into the + input, and R2 = R3 make the amplifier subtract the input (U1 has no poles: only its gain):\nout = 2·V(+) − in = in · (2 / (1 + sRC) − 1), that is, H(s) = V(out) / V(in) = (1 − sRC) / (1 + sRC).\n|H| = 1 at every frequency and the phase goes from 0 to −180° (−90° at 1.59 kHz). The pole is at s = −1/RC and the zero at s = +1/RC,\nits mirror image on the right half-plane. Step: out starts at −1 (C1 holds + at 0) and goes to +1.
